# {{PACK_NAME}}

A Kindgi pack — scaffolded by `kindgi init --template=minimal`.

Empty by design: the four discovery folders exist but ship no primitives.
Author your first via `defineTool` / `defineAgent` / `defineCheck` /
`defineFlow` from `@kindgi/sdk` — hover the exports for JSDoc.

## Layout

```
{{PACK_NAME}}/
├── kindgi.config.ts    # pack id + version + discovery patterns
├── package.json           # depends on @kindgi/sdk + zod
├── tsconfig.json
├── .claude/skills/        # SDK skills — Claude Code auto-loads per task
├── tools/                 # place `<name>/index.ts` per tool
├── agents/                # place `<name>/index.ts` per agent
├── guardrails/            # place `<name>/index.ts` per check
└── flows/                # place `<name>/index.ts` per flow
```

## AI coding assistants

`.claude/skills/` is auto-populated at `kindgi init` with per-primitive
guides: `kindgi-authoring-tools`, `kindgi-authoring-agents`,
`kindgi-authoring-guardrails`, `kindgi-getting-started` — plus
`kindgi-authoring-providers` (a real model), `kindgi-authoring-mcp-servers`
and `kindgi-framework-feedback`. Claude Code
loads them on-demand based on what you're editing — no configuration
needed. Read them directly if you want the mental model without an
assistant in the loop.

## Run

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm typecheck              # verify the pack compiles
kindgi dev                  # runs the Kindgi runtime (Docker) + hot-reloads this pack
```

The api-server ships with a built-in `demo.echo-agent` you can hit to
verify boot before authoring anything:

```sh
kindgi runs start --agent=demo.echo-agent --input='{"userMessage":"hi"}'
```

## Use a real model

`kindgi dev` gives a new pack `dev-echo`, a fallback provider that calls the
first tool and replies "Tool responded: …" — it answers only while no other
provider fits. To use Claude, with `kindgi dev` running, from another terminal:

```sh
kindgi secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY --env=local --scope=tenant   # no-echo prompt; writes .env.local
kindgi providers register --preset=anthropic                      # Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 4.5
```

Claude takes over from dev-echo on the next turn; nothing to restart.
`--models=claude-haiku-4-5` registers one model only; `kindgi providers
presets` lists the presets (Gemini on Vertex AI too). Picking a model per
agent, and other providers: `.claude/skills/kindgi-authoring-providers/SKILL.md`.

## Note on `@kindgi/sdk` versioning

This template pins `@kindgi/sdk: "workspace:*"` because the SDK is not
yet published to npm. Until it is, add the pack to a pnpm workspace that
contains the Kindgi packages (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`).
